# ◈ packages.xlibre.list — XLibre fork + suckless desktop
#
# Alternative to packages.xorg.list, not an addition to it. XLibre forked
# from Xorg in 2025 after a dispute over code quality/maintenance of
# recent Xorg contributions. Checked and confirmed (not assumed):
#   - XLibre is NOT in Gentoo's main tree — requires the X11Libre/ports-gentoo
#     overlay (or a fork of it), added by build-packages.yml only for this
#     matrix group.
#   - x11-base/xlibre-server file-collides with x11-base/xorg-server. The
#     overlay's own docs require removing xorg-server/xorg-drivers before
#     installing xlibre-server on a real system. This isn't a problem for
#     CI (each matrix group builds in its own fresh, disposable container,
#     so there's never a moment both are installed together) — it matters
#     for whoever consumes this binhost: pick ONE of xorg-server or
#     xlibre-server to actually install, not both.
#   - x11-base/xlibre-drivers is the overlay's meta-package for the driver
#     set, used here instead of xf86-input-libinput directly since XLibre's
#     driver packaging doesn't necessarily mirror Xorg's 1:1.
#   - Ebuilds in this overlay are commonly ~arch (testing) only, not
#     stable-keyworded — build-packages.yml accepts ~amd64 for this group's
#     atoms specifically, not system-wide.
#
# Less proven than packages.xorg.list — a young fork, smaller community,
# less mileage under musl specifically. Worth treating xorg-server as the
# default and xlibre-server as the opt-in experiment until it's had more
# real-world runtime.

x11-base/xlibre-server
x11-base/xlibre-drivers

x11-wm/dwm
x11-terms/st
x11-misc/dmenu
